            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for a cloth, then the Russian for to wipe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: стирка",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "стирка (stírka) — \"laundry, washing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Стирка занимает у меня целый вечер. Stírka zanimáyet u menyá tsélyy vécher. Doing the laundry takes me a whole evening."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "стирка (stírka) is built on стирать 'to wash clothes', first 'to rub off', from the root of тереть 'to rub'; EtymDB has no entry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
